WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.727
Welcome to Oakhaven!

2
00:00:03.727 --> 00:00:09.695
In this video you will learn how to play by watching a real game against the computer, step by step.

3
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.340
Two villages grow side by side for three years, one round per season.

4
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:21.187
You build outward from your Keep, take in travellers, and keep everyone fed, housed, warm and paid.

5
00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.004
Every night a creature attacks both villages.

6
00:00:24.004 --> 00:00:27.668
After twelve rounds, the village with the most points wins.

7
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.564
This is the home page.

8
00:00:32.564 --> 00:00:37.081
The Game lobby button at the top left takes you back to all the board games.

9
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.119
First pick your opponent: the computer, a friend on the same device, or Online,

10
00:00:43.119 --> 00:00:45.915
where you challenge another Ahrens Labs player.

11
00:00:45.915 --> 00:00:51.947
Online games can be quick, with two minutes per turn, or long, where you take your turn whenever you like.

12
00:00:53.960 --> 00:01:00.724
Choose how strong the computer is, from Easy up to Brutal, where the computer also starts with extra supplies.

13
00:01:00.724 --> 00:01:04.601
Then name your village and pick who goes first. We will go first.

14
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.713
Across the top you can see the twelve seasons. We are in Spring of year one.

15
00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:21.404
Two seasons each year bring an event, but which ones stays a secret until the event arrives.

16
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.065
Below that are the threats. Tonight a Wolf pack, strength three, attacks our south side.

17
00:01:28.065 --> 00:01:31.431
Our defense is only one, so right now we would lose.

18
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.047
You can only see part of what is coming.

19
00:01:35.047 --> 00:01:40.360
Next round’s creature is shown, but not which side it will hit, unless you have a Watchtower.

20
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:44.877
The one after that is a mystery card until an Archer works in your tower.

21
00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.345
These are the locations.

22
00:01:48.345 --> 00:01:53.232
Each game uses five, drawn from twenty, so every game is a little different.

23
00:01:53.232 --> 00:01:58.005
Each one holds just one worker per round, so whoever gets there first takes it.

24
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.623
The sixth one, the Work crew, is in every game.

25
00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:07.147
It finishes everything you have under construction straight away, so it works tonight,

26
00:02:07.147 --> 00:02:09.787
and frees your builders to work or build again.

27
00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:16.292
Below them are two always-open places, the Village commons and Odd jobs.

28
00:02:16.292 --> 00:02:22.004
They give much less, but any number of workers can go there, so a spare worker is never wasted.

29
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:29.793
This is your village: thirty-seven hexes in three rings around your Keep, so there is plenty of room to grow.

30
00:02:29.793 --> 00:02:36.664
Meadows take farms or town buildings, forests take lumber camps, hills take quarries and mountains take mines.

31
00:02:36.664 --> 00:02:39.887
You start with a Keep in the middle, a Farm and two Peasants.

32
00:02:39.887 --> 00:02:45.343
Every new building must touch one you already have, so your village grows from the inside out.

33
00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.729
Your stores are on the right: food, wood, stone, iron and gold.

34
00:02:52.729 --> 00:02:58.064
The panel also warns you if supper, wages or tonight’s fight are going to go badly.

35
00:02:58.064 --> 00:03:00.683
Scores stay secret until the very end.

36
00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.489
Each year also has three goals.

37
00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:08.373
This year they are Full larder, Green fields and Armed to the teeth.

38
00:03:08.373 --> 00:03:10.551
They only count what you do this year,

39
00:03:10.551 --> 00:03:15.096
and after Winter the village that did the most on each one scores four points.

40
00:03:15.096 --> 00:03:18.013
Then three new goals are revealed for the next year.

41
00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.180
Each round you get two workers.

42
00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:27.792
On your turn you send one worker to an empty location and get its reward right away.

43
00:03:27.792 --> 00:03:33.099
That ends your turn. Let’s send one to the Hunting grounds for three food and two wood.

44
00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:39.313
Now the computer takes its turn, and it places a worker too.

45
00:03:39.313 --> 00:03:43.276
Watch the locations and the chronicle at the bottom of the page.

46
00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:49.213
The computer went to the Work crew. That spot is now blocked for us this round.

47
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.865
Besides workers, you have free actions. You can do as many as you can pay for,

48
00:03:54.865 --> 00:03:59.603
before or after placing a worker: build, put up walls, mount crossbows,

49
00:03:59.603 --> 00:04:02.563
recruit travellers, train villagers and trade.

50
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:09.903
First, the wolf pack. A Palisade costs two wood and adds two defense on one side.

51
00:04:09.903 --> 00:04:13.396
On the south side, that makes three, and we drive them off.

52
00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:19.839
Next, more food. Click Build to see every building, what it costs and what it does.

53
00:04:19.839 --> 00:04:21.888
At the top you choose who builds it.

54
00:04:21.888 --> 00:04:25.772
The builder leaves their job, and an idle villager steps into it.

55
00:04:25.772 --> 00:04:31.661
Builders don’t work or defend until their building is finished, so the game suggests our idle Peasant.

56
00:04:31.661 --> 00:04:33.811
A Farm costs just one wood.

57
00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.433
Pick it, then choose a glowing meadow. Only spots touching your village glow.

58
00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:45.424
Where you build matters: Farms next to a Well make one more food,

59
00:04:45.424 --> 00:04:49.536
and valuable buildings are safer in the middle, away from the walls.

60
00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.863
See the hammer sign? New buildings are under construction until next season.

61
00:04:55.863 --> 00:04:59.533
They make nothing yet, and add no beds, water or defense.

62
00:04:59.533 --> 00:05:02.408
The builder’s portrait shows who is working on it.

63
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.884
Down here is the Crossroads, where travellers wait for a new home.

64
00:05:07.884 --> 00:05:10.872
The first in line is cheapest but leaves tonight.

65
00:05:10.872 --> 00:05:15.880
This Farmer costs only one gold, and makes more food than a Peasant on a Farm.

66
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.305
Every villager needs a bed and water.

67
00:05:20.305 --> 00:05:23.528
We have room for one more, so let’s take the Farmer in.

68
00:05:23.528 --> 00:05:28.131
New villagers take a free job right away, and a Farmer heads for a Farm.

69
00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.244
Can’t find the person you want at the Crossroads?

70
00:05:32.244 --> 00:05:35.829
Once a round, you can train one of your Peasants into any trade.

71
00:05:35.829 --> 00:05:40.204
It costs that trade’s full price plus two gold, but they already have a bed,

72
00:05:40.204 --> 00:05:42.631
and they move straight into their own building.

73
00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.487
Short of something?

74
00:05:46.487 --> 00:05:51.437
Trading is free too: two of anything for one of anything else, as often as you like.

75
00:05:51.437 --> 00:05:54.803
A Merchant, or the Trading post, makes it one for one.

76
00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:00.057
Now our second worker. We’ll take the Militia yard.

77
00:06:00.057 --> 00:06:06.665
Because it is our last worker, our turn doesn’t end: we can still use free actions, and then press End round.

78
00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:13.555
When you are done, press End round. Any worker you didn’t place is lost, so use them both!

79
00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.519
Once both villages have ended the round, night falls.

80
00:06:20.519 --> 00:06:25.384
First every worked building produces. Then the creature attacks both villages.

81
00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:31.096
With the palisade and the militia our defense held, so we win the wolves’ trophy, worth one point.

82
00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.303
Then supper: every villager eats one food.

83
00:06:36.303 --> 00:06:41.168
If you are short, villagers leave and you lose points. In Winter, farms rest,

84
00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:43.473
every three villagers burn one wood,

85
00:06:43.473 --> 00:06:47.208
and each palisade needs one wood of repairs or it falls.

86
00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:53.581
And on the night before each Spring, you pay every working villager one gold, and the year’s goals are scored.

87
00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:00.637
Finally the front traveller leaves the Crossroads, and new ones arrive.

88
00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.948
In Summer the computer goes first, because the first player switches every round.

89
00:07:10.948 --> 00:07:15.024
Now tonight’s creature shows its side, and the next card moves up.

90
00:07:15.024 --> 00:07:20.188
Flying creatures come over the walls, so against them you need Archers, a Watchtower,

91
00:07:20.188 --> 00:07:22.423
the Militia yard, or crossbows.

92
00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:28.729
A crossbow, for two wood and one iron, sits on one of your walls.

93
00:07:28.729 --> 00:07:34.021
It adds four defense against flyers coming from that side, but it falls if its wall does.

94
00:07:34.021 --> 00:07:38.859
And once a side has a Stone wall, you can upgrade it to Iron for six defense.

95
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:46.020
This is one of the event seasons. Both villages face the same event, Pilgrims,

96
00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.203
but each makes its own choice, and you must choose before you can end the round.

97
00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:54.656
There is always at least one option you can afford. We’ll pick Ask a tithe.

98
00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.647
Now let’s go through every rule.

99
00:07:58.647 --> 00:08:03.128
The rules are always one click away, from the Rules button in the top bar.

100
00:08:03.128 --> 00:08:07.048
The first tab is this video, so you can come back to it any time.

101
00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.953
The Basics tab explains where you build. Every building must touch one you already have,

102
00:08:13.953 --> 00:08:17.731
and distance matters: towers only guard the sides near them,

103
00:08:17.731 --> 00:08:21.971
and a creature that breaks through burns whatever is closest to its side.

104
00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.777
Each round has three parts.

105
00:08:25.777 --> 00:08:31.304
In the morning each village gets its workers: two, or three once a Steward works your Keep.

106
00:08:31.304 --> 00:08:36.013
In the day you take turns. At dusk the night plays out for both villages.

107
00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:43.287
On your turn you can do any number of free actions, then place one worker, or press End round.

108
00:08:43.287 --> 00:08:48.316
Once you end the round you are done until tomorrow, and unplaced workers are wasted.

109
00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:52.911
Anything a place gives you for tonight or this round,

110
00:08:52.911 --> 00:08:56.219
like the Militia yard’s defense or the Tavern’s discount,

111
00:08:56.219 --> 00:08:58.475
wears off when the next round starts.

112
00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:05.244
The seasons matter. In Summer worked farms make one more food, and in Autumn two more.

113
00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:12.193
In Winter farms make nothing, every three villagers burn one wood to stay warm, and palisades need mending.

114
00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:19.780
Workers and places lists all twenty main places in five groups: food, materials,

115
00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.875
coin and trade, people and renown, and defense.

116
00:09:22.875 --> 00:09:27.520
Each game uses one from every group, marked with a tick, plus the Work crew.

117
00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.217
Each main place holds one worker per round, from either village.

118
00:09:33.217 --> 00:09:36.049
You get the reward the moment you place the worker.

119
00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:42.265
At the bottom are the two always-open places, the Village commons and Odd jobs.

120
00:09:42.265 --> 00:09:48.489
They give just one food or one gold, but there is no limit, even for several of your own workers.

121
00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:53.017
The fine print covers every special case,

122
00:09:53.017 --> 00:09:55.963
like the Moneylender taking your points below zero,

123
00:09:55.963 --> 00:10:01.269
or how the Mason’s lodge raises tonight’s wall and then one more side of your choice.

124
00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.991
Free actions need no worker.

125
00:10:04.991 --> 00:10:09.408
Build as many buildings as you can pay for and have free villagers to build,

126
00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:12.972
on a free hex of the right land, next to one of your buildings.

127
00:10:12.972 --> 00:10:18.157
Walls defend only their own side: a palisade costs two wood for two defense,

128
00:10:18.157 --> 00:10:20.953
stone costs three stone more for four in total,

129
00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:24.453
and iron costs one stone and two iron more for six.

130
00:10:24.453 --> 00:10:28.288
A crossbow on a wall adds four against flyers from that side.

131
00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:36.791
You can also train one Peasant a round, trade two of anything for one of anything else,

132
00:10:36.791 --> 00:10:40.177
and move villagers between jobs at any time on your turn.

133
00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:47.607
At the Crossroads, the first traveller costs two gold less, and the second one less, but never below one.

134
00:10:47.607 --> 00:10:49.720
Taking someone moves the line up.

135
00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:53.561
It only refills at night, when the front traveller leaves for good.

136
00:10:53.561 --> 00:10:56.457
A Peasant for one gold is always available.

137
00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:02.332
Each traveller has a trade and works best in their own building.

138
00:11:02.332 --> 00:11:05.853
Anyone can work a farm, lumber camp, quarry or mine.

139
00:11:05.853 --> 00:11:09.837
Each building holds one worker, except the Barracks, which holds two.

140
00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:16.303
At night, in order: buildings work, Blacksmiths forge arms, the creature attacks,

141
00:11:16.303 --> 00:11:20.613
everyone eats supper, in Winter you burn firewood and mend palisades,

142
00:11:20.613 --> 00:11:24.476
before Spring you pay wages, and then the Crossroads changes.

143
00:11:24.476 --> 00:11:29.633
For every food, wood or gold you are short, a villager leaves and you lose a point.

144
00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:37.295
Your defense adds up: one from the Keep, one per set of arms, your Guards and Knights,

145
00:11:37.295 --> 00:11:42.736
the wall on the side being attacked, and anything tonight’s places gave you. Watchtowers,

146
00:11:42.736 --> 00:11:49.671
the Wizard’s Tower and the Archers and Wizard inside them only count if the attack comes from a side close enough.

147
00:11:49.671 --> 00:11:53.100
Flyers ignore walls, but not the crossbows on them.

148
00:11:56.040 --> 00:12:00.863
If your defense is at least the creature’s strength, you drive it off and win its trophy.

149
00:12:00.863 --> 00:12:05.408
If not, it might take resources, knock down a wall, carry off a villager,

150
00:12:05.408 --> 00:12:10.075
turn one to stone, or burn a building. This table explains each one.

151
00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.255
Goals and events have their own tab.

152
00:12:14.255 --> 00:12:20.073
It lists all twelve goals, with this year’s three ticked, and every event with all of its choices.

153
00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:25.929
The Buildings tab shows every building, its cost, its land and its points.

154
00:12:25.929 --> 00:12:29.280
Buildings with a job only score while someone works there.

155
00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:34.679
Houses sleep four, and Wells give water for five more villagers. Neighbours matter too:

156
00:12:34.679 --> 00:12:39.139
a House next to a Chapel scores a point, but next to a noisy Smithy,

157
00:12:39.139 --> 00:12:41.672
Barracks or Market it sleeps one fewer.

158
00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:49.295
Three buildings are wonders: the Castle, the Wizard’s Tower and the Cathedral.

159
00:12:49.295 --> 00:12:54.089
Only one village can build each, and you need five or seven villagers first.

160
00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:00.513
The Villagers tab shows all seventeen kinds of traveller: their price, what they do,

161
00:13:00.513 --> 00:13:05.393
where they work and their points. A Steward gives you an extra worker every round.

162
00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:11.279
Round one is always the Wolf pack. Creatures get stronger every year:

163
00:13:11.279 --> 00:13:14.971
strength three or four in year one, seven to nine in year two,

164
00:13:14.971 --> 00:13:17.397
and thirteen or fourteen in year three.

165
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:23.247
Every creature attacks from one side, shown on the map once you can see it.

166
00:13:23.247 --> 00:13:27.259
Flyers come over the walls, so only a crossbow on that wall helps.

167
00:13:27.259 --> 00:13:32.075
Each card shows the trophy for driving it off, and the damage if it breaks through.

168
00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:38.049
At the end, points come from renown, staffed buildings, villagers,

169
00:13:38.049 --> 00:13:44.429
one per stone or iron wall, three for walls on all six sides, one per five leftover gold,

170
00:13:44.429 --> 00:13:47.033
and everything you won from the yearly goals.

171
00:13:47.033 --> 00:13:50.228
On a tie, the village with more villagers wins.

172
00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:56.035
And at the bottom are some strategy tips to get you started.

173
00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:01.409
Let’s skip ahead to the end of year three.

174
00:14:01.409 --> 00:14:06.865
Scores stay hidden all game, so the end is a big reveal, one category at a time.

175
00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:17.044
Each category is added up for both villages, and the winner is crowned at the end.

176
00:14:17.044 --> 00:14:20.772
From here you can start a new game, or go back to the lobby.

177
00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:27.617
Remember: watch tonight’s threat, keep food for Winter and gold for wages,

178
00:14:27.617 --> 00:14:33.123
build outward with care, and use every worker each round. Your game saves as you play,

179
00:14:33.123 --> 00:14:35.876
and when you are signed in it is kept in your account,

180
00:14:35.876 --> 00:14:38.160
so you can carry on from any device.

181
00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:42.343
You can keep several games going from Your games on the Board Game Shelf.

182
00:14:42.343 --> 00:14:46.077
To play a friend online, pick Online when you start a new game.

183
00:14:46.077 --> 00:14:48.739
Good luck, and have fun building your village!

